Hello and welcome! If you haven't already, please read through the
Support Template
, it will help others help you more effectively. In this case, what plugins you are using is relevant.
In any case, the code that you showed should throw an error (you're missing a closing curly for the second if clause). So if you say that the level up message hasn't changed (meaning that it didn't crash on load) my first suspicion is that the plugin hasn't been loaded at all.
EDIT: also, the code you showed is for the status window. So it won't affect how the level shows up in the level up message. To tweak the message, one way of doing it is to tweak the displayLevelUp function, for example:
JavaScript:
Game_Actor.prototype.displayLevelUp = function(newSkills) {
    const text = TextManager.levelUp.format(
        this._name,
        TextManager.level,
//Array with ranks, pick the index equal to numerical level minus one
        ['Novice','Knight'][this._level-1]
//Original code
//        this._level
        );
    $gameMessage.newPage();
    $gameMessage.add(text);
    for (const skill of newSkills) {
        $gameMessage.add(TextManager.obtainSkill.format(skill.name));
    }
};
It will work if you just add more ranks to the array like ['Novice','Squire','Knight','Hero'], but do note that it's probably better to make it read a class note tag.

Hope it works! If you need a notetagged version (basically you list the level names in the notes in the class and the plugin will pick up the list from there), I can add that in and combine this one and the kind stranger plugin into a single plugin.
As with the code that I showed above, the kind stranger plugin can also be condensed as follows:
JavaScript:
Window_StatusBase.prototype.drawActorLevel = function(actor, x, y) {
    const levelName = ['Novice','Knight'][actor._level-1];
    this.drawText(levelName, x, y, 36, "right");
};
